<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 8 May, from 1559 to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1559 CE <span class="tih-ago">467 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elizabeth I's Act of Supremacy receives royal assent</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Act restored the Church of England's independence from Rome and made Elizabeth its Supreme Governor. With the Act of Uniformity it formed the basis of the Elizabethan religious settlement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1794 CE <span class="tih-ago">232 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chemist Antoine Lavoisier is guillotined in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lavoisier, executed as a former tax farmer during the Terror, had named oxygen and hydrogen and set chemistry on modern foundations. 'It took them only an instant to cut off that head,' said Lagrange.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1846 CE <span class="tih-ago">180 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US and Mexican armies clash at Palo Alto</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Zachary Taylor's artillery won the first major battle of the Mexican-American War near the Rio Grande. By 1848 Mexico had lost about half its territory, including California.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1886 CE <span class="tih-ago">140 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Coca-Cola goes on sale at an Atlanta pharmacy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pharmacist John Pemberton's new syrup, mixed with carbonated water, was sold at Jacobs' Pharmacy for five cents a glass. It became one of the most widely recognised brands in the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 CE <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Allies celebrate Victory in Europe Day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Germany's surrender took effect and crowds filled the streets of London, Paris and New York. In Moscow, where the surrender came after midnight, victory is marked on 9 May.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1963 CE <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Troops fire on Buddhist protesters in Huế</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">South Vietnamese forces fired on crowds protesting a ban on Buddhist flags, killing nine. The Buddhist crisis that followed undermined President Ngo Dinh Diem, who was overthrown in November.</p></div></li></ol>
